VFTP @VERSION@ for OpenVMS (vms-vftp, @ARCH@) - EARLY TEST RELEASE
=================================================================

VFTP is a full-screen FTP, SFTP and SCP client: the local directory and a
server's in two framed panes, with the LK201 keys, PF1 as the GOLD key and
one-letter commands. It looks like VTREE (vms-vtree) and VLMF (vms-vlmf).

    SFTP   by libssh2 (linked into VFTP.EXE), to any SSH server
    SCP    files by scp, listing and the rest by shell commands: Unix servers
           only (a VMS sshd has no Unix shell; use SFTP there)
    FTP    plain or FTPS (AUTH TLS, explicit), passive mode

Starting it
-----------
VFTP$SETUP.COM defines the VFTP command; a system manager can run it for
everyone from SYS$MANAGER:SYLOGIN.COM:
    $ @VFTP$ROOT:[000000]VFTP$SETUP.COM

    $ VFTP                       ! the Open form, empty
    $ VFTP user@host:port        ! the Open form filled in
    $ VFTP mysite                ! a saved site (L)

It needs a VT100-compatible terminal of at least 20 x 80. On a terminal
without colour, DEFINE VFTP$DISPLAY MONO first. Help (or PF2) lists the keys;
F10 or Ctrl/Z leaves.

The keys
--------
  Up/Down, Prev/Next    move; GOLD Up/Down first/last
  Tab                   the other pane (local / remote)
  Return, Select, Right open the directory; on a file: View
  Left, -, Backspace    up one directory
  J                     jump to a directory (a VMS spec or a path)
  O                     open a connection (SFTP, SCP or FTP); GOLD O closes it
  L                     saved sites: open one, or save the Open form's
  G, P                  Get (download), Put (upload) the tagged or current
                        entries; a directory goes whole, with all that is in it
  C, F5                 copy to the other pane (Get or Put)
  D, Remove             delete (asks first)
  R, M, V, A            rename, make a directory, view, attributes
  GOLD A                a server's permissions: 644, rw-r--r--, go-w
  T, Space              tag/untag; GOLD T all, GOLD U none, * by name
  X                     transfer mode: AUTO, ASCII, BINARY
  S, F                  sort, filter; GOLD V every version / highest only
  GOLD W, Ctrl/W        read both panes again; redraw
  F10, Ctrl/Z, Ctrl/C   cancel a transfer

Text and binary
---------------
In AUTO mode a Put sends a file as text when it has variable or VFC records
with carriage control, each record a line; a Get takes a file as text when
its type is in VFTP$TEXT_TYPES (default .TXT .C .COM .HTML and others). Text
arrives as variable-length records; binary as fixed 512-byte records when
its size is a multiple of 512, otherwise as undefined records.

Safety
------
- A download is always a new version: no local file is ever replaced.
- A Put of a name the server has already, or a delete anywhere, shows what
  would change and asks first; the default is No. On a server without
  versions a Put goes to a temporary name and replaces the file only when it
  has arrived whole, so a cancel leaves the old file as it was.
- An SSH server's key is checked against SYS$LOGIN:[.SSH]KNOWN_HOSTS, as ssh
  does: an unknown one shows its fingerprint and asks; a changed one is
  refused. An FTPS server's certificate is pinned in [.SSH]VFTP_KNOWN_TLS.
- Plain FTP sends the password in the clear: VFTP asks before it does.
- Passwords are never stored: not in the sites file, not in the log.
- Every operation is logged in VFTP$LOG (default SYS$LOGIN:VFTP.LOG).

Logging in
----------
SSH: a key in SYS$LOGIN:[.SSH] (ID_ED25519, ID_ECDSA, ID_RSA, as ssh's) when
the server takes it, else a password typed into the form. FTP: a password.

Resuming
--------
A binary Get or Put by SFTP, or by FTP to a server whose FEAT lists REST
STREAM, goes through a half file (NAME.EXT_VFTP-PART here, name.vftp-part
on the server) that becomes the real file at the end. A transfer that is
cancelled or fails keeps it; the next Get or Put of the file asks whether to
go on from it (Y or Return), start again (N) or copy nothing. Text, SCP and
FTP to a server without REST (the VMS FTP servers) start again.

Files and logical names
-----------------------
  VFTP$SITES       the sites file (default SYS$LOGIN:VFTP.SITES)
  VFTP$LOG         the log (default SYS$LOGIN:VFTP.LOG)
  VFTP$TEXT_TYPES  file types a Get takes as text, e.g. ".TXT,.LIS,.LOG"
  VFTP$DISPLAY     MONO for a terminal without colour

What is installed
-----------------
    VFTP$ROOT:[000000]VFTP.EXE, VFTP$SETUP.COM, README.VMS, LICENSE.
    VFTP$ROOT:[000000]LIBSSH2-COPYING.   libssh2's licence (it is linked in)
    SYS$STARTUP:VFTP$STARTUP.COM         defines VFTP$ROOT and VFTP

VFTP needs VSI's SSL3 kit (V3.0 or later) and no privileges.

    https://github.com/issinoho/vms-vftp
